From 1cca31bb9aaf8dcc1f4219461dcb88cacc8663c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:19:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/22] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: pdphy: don't log a sent
 hard reset as an error

PMIC_PDPHY_SIG_TX_IRQ fires when a hard reset signal has gone out, which
is ordinary: TCPM sends two to any partner that does not answer with
source capabilities, such as a PC port without USB PD. Every such attach
logged two "isr: tx_sig" lines at error level for a working connection.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c
index c8b1463e6..1dfa8dbc7 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c
@@ -380,7 +380,7 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy_isr(int irq, void *dev_id)
 
 	switch (irq_data->virq) {
 	case PMIC_PDPHY_SIG_TX_IRQ:
-		dev_err(dev, "isr: tx_sig\n");
+		dev_dbg(dev, "isr: tx_sig\n");
 		break;
 	case PMIC_PDPHY_SIG_RX_IRQ:
 		schedule_work(&pmic_typec_pdphy->reset_work);
-- 
